# apps.rst, thread_latency (M3): sem, nopreempt mode.
# Schematic: 1 unit is 1 pixel; the box widths fit the labels, they are
# not durations. The masks are those of the pinned trees (both the same).
include apps.tdc
diagram thread-latency-nopreempt "thread_latency, sem-nopreempt: the taker runs only when the giver blocks"
schematic
prio taker 3
axis "time after the giver wakes (schematic)" -30..607

taker pending -30.. "blocked in k_sem_take()"
giver -30..0 : The ISR of the edge woke the giver. The giver took t_thr.
at 0
giver 36 "now" : t0 = stim_now(), just before the wake call.
@t0
giver 43 "give" {basepri} : k_sem_give() makes the taker ready, with the semaphore spinlock (BASEPRI). The taker has the lower priority, so there is no switch.
giver 36 "now" : t2 = stim_now(): the wake call has returned.
@t2
giver 56 "record" : The giver records t2t and t2t_ret of the previous edge, then calls giver_prepare().
giver 82 "stim_arm()" {basepri} : Programs the next edge, with irq_lock() (BASEPRI).
giver 43 "take" {basepri} : k_sem_take(&isr_sem) blocks, with BASEPRI until arch_swap() pends PendSV and unlocks.
@giver_blocks anchor
giver pending giver_blocks..607 "blocked in k_sem_take(isr_sem)"
pendsv 56 "switch" {basepri 16..40} : PendSV, giver to taker. BASEPRI while it takes the next thread from the ready queue cache.
taker 36 "now" : t1 = stim_now(), the first action after k_sem_take() returns.
@t1
taker 43 "take" {basepri} : The taker counts the wake. k_sem_take() blocks again, with BASEPRI until arch_swap().
@taker_blocks anchor
taker pending taker_blocks..607 "blocked"
pendsv 56 "switch" {basepri 16..40} : PendSV, taker to the idle thread.
idle 49 "idle" {basepri} : The idle thread continues after cpsie, in the idle loop: arch_irq_lock() sets BASEPRI. Then k_cpu_idle() sets PRIMASK and clears BASEPRI.
@sleeps anchor
idle sleep sleeps..607 "WFI" {primask}
span t0..t2 "t2t_ret" !
span t0..t1 "t2t" !
